Equating the coefficient of $x$ to zero.
$\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow \quad x^{\mathrm{r} / 2} \cdot \mathrm{x}^{-2(10-\mathrm{r})}=\mathrm{x}^0 \\
& \Rightarrow \quad \frac{\mathrm{r}}{2}-20+2 \mathrm{r}=0 \\
& \Rightarrow \quad \frac{5}{2} \mathrm{r}=20 \Rightarrow \mathrm{r}=8
\end{aligned}\begin{aligned}
\text { Coefficient } & ={ }^{10} \mathrm{C}_{\mathrm{r}}\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{10-\mathrm{r}} \\
& ={ }^{10} \mathrm{C}_8\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{10-8}
\end{aligned}=\frac{10 \times 9}{2} \times \frac{1}{9}=5$

